# Adding a compare / alternatives competitor

Ship **one new competitor constant** plus **registry and UI wiring** in the same change.

| Product line | Reference constant | Compare detail layout |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Social scheduler | **`scheduler/hootsuite.ts`**, **`scheduler/buffer.ts`** | `social_matrix` (feature matrix + channels) |
| Directory submission service | **`submission/boringlaunch.ts`** | `directory_long_form` (sticky section nav + long-form sections) |

OpenQuok’s own entry is **`scheduler/openquok.ts`** (special — see below). OpenQuok lists **both** categories so it can pair with schedulers and directory services.

Competitor data powers:

| Surface | Route | Behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Compare hub | `/compare` | Two sections — **Social media schedulers** and **Directory submission services** — each with OpenQuok as base and category-scoped dropdown + cards |
| Compare detail | `/compare/{productA}/{productB}` | Head-to-head when `getComparePair` succeeds (same category overlap); **404** on cross-category pairs (e.g. Buffer vs BoringLaunch) |
| Alternatives hub | `/alternatives` | Social and directory sections; pinned **OpenQuok alternatives** card in the social section; competitor cards from `ALTERNATIVES_TARGET_SLUGS`; category, sort, and search query params (`alternativesHubFilters.ts`) |
| Alternatives detail | `/alternatives/{slug}` | Long-form sections + sticky **On this page** nav when `directoryLongForm` or default social long-form applies; ranked listings; OpenQuok #1 on competitor targets; **`/alternatives/openquok`** lists comparable peers (schedulers + directory) without OpenQuok as a peer row |

**No new route files** are required for compare or alternatives when adding a competitor — only data + the manual steps below.

Follow **source-project-neutrality**: describe products and positioning in first-party terms; trademark notes belong only in `branded-icons.ts` where needed.

**User-facing copy** (competitor constants, compare/alternatives presenters, and compare/alternatives route pages): write in **ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English**. Use short sentences. Put one idea in each sentence. Use active voice. Address the reader as **you**. Use plain words. Do not explain in the copy (or in chat) that you follow this style.

---

## Identifier contract

Use one **lowercase kebab-case** slug everywhere:

- `CompareProduct.slug` and `CompareProductSlug` union member
- Filename: `web/src/lib/content/constants/competitors/scheduler/{slug}.ts` for social schedulers (including **`scheduler/openquok.ts`**); `web/src/lib/content/constants/competitors/submission/{slug}.ts` for directory submission services
- Export name: `{slug}CompareProduct` (e.g. `hootsuiteCompareProduct`)
- URLs: `/compare/openquok/{slug}`, `/alternatives/{slug}`
- `COMPARE_PRODUCT_WEBSITE_URLS` key
- Branded icon registry key (PascalCase, e.g. `Hootsuite` → `icons.Hootsuite.name`)

Do **not** add `openquok` to **`ALTERNATIVES_TARGET_SLUGS`** — that array drives auto-generated competitor hub cards only. OpenQuok still has a **manual** hub card (`buildOpenQuokHubEntry`) and a public detail route via **`isAlternativesTargetSlug('openquok')`** and **`listAlternativeProductsFor('openquok')`**.

