## Required files (manual)

### 1. Branded icon

**`web/src/data/icons/branded-icons.ts`**

- Add `IconName` union entry and `icons.{Brand}` object (inline SVG preferred).
- See **company-brand-icons** rule.

### 2. Slug type and categories

**`web/src/lib/content/constants/competitors/types.ts`**

- Extend `CompareProductSlug` with the new slug literal.
- `CompareProductCategory`: `'social_scheduling' | 'directory_submission'`.
- Every `CompareProduct` needs `categories: readonly CompareProductCategory[]`:
  - **OpenQuok**: both (`COMPARE_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_OPENQUOK` in `shared.ts`).
  - **Social schedulers**: `['social_scheduling']` only (`COMPARE_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_SOCIAL_SCHEDULING`).
  - **Directory services**: `['directory_submission']` only (`COMPARE_PRODUCT_CATEGORIES_DIRECTORY_SUBMISSION`).

**Pair rules** (`utils/compareProductCategories.ts`):

- `canCompareProducts(a, b)` — false for same slug; true when category sets **intersect** (OpenQuok vs any peer in a shared category).
- `getComparePair` / `buildComparePair` return `null` when `!canCompareProducts` (invalid URLs 404).
- `listComparePairsForHub(baseSlug, category)` and `listCompareProductsForHubDropdown(category)` scope hub sections.
- `resolveComparePairLayout` → `directory_long_form` when the pair is directory-focused (directory-only competitor vs OpenQuok); else `social_matrix`.

### 3. Competitor constant (new file)

**`web/src/lib/content/constants/competitors/scheduler/{slug}.ts`** or **`web/src/lib/content/constants/competitors/submission/{slug}.ts`** (see **Identifier contract**)

Export a `CompareProduct` with:

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `slug`, `name`, `icon` | `icon: icons.{Brand}.name` |
| `categories` | See **Slug type and categories** — required on every product |
| `tagline` | Short subtitle under the name on compare pages (ASD-STE100) |
| `overview` | **Two or three short sentences** for platform overview and alternatives listings. Use simple words. One idea per sentence. Put pricing tiers, verify disclaimers, and feature lists in `tagline`, `pricingPlans`, or long-form sections — not here. |
| `pricingPlans` | `ComparePricingPlan[]` — public list prices in USD; `monthlyPrice: null` for custom/enterprise; add a **Self-host** row at `$0` when the vendor ships AGPL/OSS self-host with no software fee; directory services use `pricePeriod: 'one_time'` on package rows |
| `pricingUnit` | Optional: `per_channel` (Buffer, Hopper HQ), `per_seat` (Hootsuite), or omit for flat workspace/account bundles |
| `channels` | **Social schedulers:** human labels aligned with `listAvailablePublicChannelCompareLabels()` in `channels/index.ts`. **Directory services:** `[]` — do not invent social lists; OpenQuok still shows **Supported social channels** on directory pairs from OpenQuok’s channel list |
| `directoryCoverageSummary` | **Directory services only:** one paragraph from the vendor’s public pricing/site when they do not publish a fixed directory list (package counts, e.g. 100/200 submissions). Powers **Supported directory channels** on compare/alternatives (OpenQuok column: PeerPush + Uneed icons) |
| `featureSupport` | `Partial<Record<PublicPricingCompareRowId, CompareFeatureCell>>` — **social:** cover social + shared rows you intend to show; **directory:** fill **`directory_*`** rows in `PUBLIC_PRICING_COMPARE_ROWS` honestly (done-for-you vs DIY); omit or use **No Info** on `official_api` when the vendor is a service, not a platform API publisher |
| `directoryLongForm` | **Directory competitors only:** `CompareDirectoryLongFormContent` (`whyPeopleLook`, `yourOptions`, `whenTheyWin`) — ASD-STE100 body copy; **two or three short sentences per section**; set each section `subtitle` to the same text as `navLabel` (matches **On this page**); merged in `buildComparePair.ts` with FAQ ids |
| `comparison` | `headline`, `notAnother`, `builtFor`, `positioningWhenLeft`, optional `withoutTitle`, and `talkingPoints` — all ASD-STE100 |

### Official platform APIs (`official_api`)

This row is **not** the same as **Public API** (`public_api`). It answers whether the product **publishes to social networks** through each platform’s **official APIs** (OAuth, Graph API, Content Posting API, official Bot API, and similar approved routes) — as opposed to browser extensions, logged-in session automation, scrapers, or other unofficial workarounds. See the tooltip on `official_api` in `PUBLIC_PRICING_COMPARE_ROWS` (`publicPricingCatalog.ts`).

**Every new competitor** (and any refresh of an existing one) must set `featureSupport.official_api` from **that vendor’s public site**, not from inference or industry reputation alone.

#### Where to look

Search and read the competitor’s **marketing site**, **help center**, **channel/integration pages**, **trust/legal pages**, and **first-party docs** on their domain (e.g. `postiz.com/channels/instagram`, `support.*`, `docs.*`, blog posts that describe how publishing works). Do not treat “we have a REST API” or “official SDK” as proof of official **platform** publishing.

#### How to set the cell

| Value | When |
| --- | --- |
| `{ kind: 'included' }` | The vendor **explicitly states** that scheduling/publishing uses official platform APIs, OAuth to the platform, Graph API / partner APIs, “official APIs only,” Meta Business Partner publishing routes, or equivalent wording tied to **posting**. |
| `{ kind: 'excluded' }` | The vendor **explicitly states** a non-official publish path (e.g. Chrome extension with an existing browser session, password login, browser automation, “no official API”). |
| `{ kind: 'text', text: 'No Info' }` | No clear publish-method statement after a reasonable pass over their site — **do not guess**. |

#### Common mistakes

- Marking **included** because the product is a well-known scheduler or a Meta partner **without** a publish-method quote on their site.
- Marking **included** because docs describe **your** integration with **their** HTTP API (`public_api`).
- Marking **excluded** without evidence; default to **No Info** when publish mechanics are undocumented.
- Confusing **analytics** (“data via the official X API”) with **publishing** unless they also state official APIs for posts.

#### PR evidence

In the PR description (or review notes), cite **one or two URLs** and a short phrase from each page that justify `included`, `excluded`, or **No Info**. No need to paste quotes into repo comments unless useful for future audits.

**Talking points** (`CompareTalkingPointId` keys in `shared.ts` → `COMPARE_TALKING_POINT_ORDER`):

- For a pair row to appear in the with/without section, the **left** product needs `strength` and the **right** product needs `weakness` for the **same** topic id.
- When OpenQuok is on the left, competitor `weakness` copy drives the “without” column.
- When a competitor is on the left vs another competitor, both need matching topic keys.
- **Directory pairs:** use directory topic ids — `submission_model`, `pace_and_control`, `dr_outcomes` (plus shared ids like `pricing_model`, `product_focus` when relevant). Extend **`scheduler/openquok.ts`** `comparison.talkingPoints` (or directory-specific strengths) so OpenQuok vs a directory service is not empty.

### 4. Registry

**`web/src/lib/content/constants/competitors/index.ts`**

- Import and re-export `{slug}CompareProduct`.
- Append to `PUBLIC_COMPARE_PRODUCTS` (keep **OpenQuok first**, then competitors alphabetically or by priority).

`ALTERNATIVES_TARGET_SLUGS`, `getCompareProduct`, `getComparePair`, `listComparePairsForHub`, and `listAlternativeProductsFor` derive from this array — no separate list to maintain.

### 5. Official website URL

**`web/src/lib/content/constants/competitors/shared.ts`**

- Add the slug to `COMPARE_PRODUCT_WEBSITE_URLS` (used for “Go to website” on alternatives detail).

### 6. Product icon styles (UI)

Add gradient ring colors for the new slug in **`web/src/lib/content/constants/competitors/compareProductIconStyles.ts`** (`BASE` map — one entry per `CompareProductSlug`). That file exports:

| Export | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `COMPARE_PRODUCT_ICON_STYLES_HUB` | Compare hub, alternatives hub (`containerClass`) |
| `COMPARE_PRODUCT_ICON_STYLES_HERO` / `COMPARE_PRODUCT_ICON_STYLES_CARD` | Compare detail cards and heroes |
| `getCompareProductHeroCardIconStyles` | Compare detail and alternatives detail (hero + card rings) |

Compare/alternatives route Svelte files import these maps — **do not** duplicate `PRODUCT_ICON_STYLES` in route files. Match the visual language of existing competitors (distinct gradient, readable icon contrast).

